# rust
#
# The upstream template, vendored here so the fold reads it from the repository and needs no
# network. The lockfile choice is the one thing it cannot express, so it follows as an optional
# block: a library ignores Cargo.lock; a binary commits it so builds reproduce.
#
# Source: github/gitignore Rust.gitignore
# Generated by Cargo
# will have compiled files and executables
debug
target

# These are backup files generated by rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk

# MSVC Windows builds of rustc generate these, which store debugging information
*.pdb

# Generated by cargo mutants
# Contains mutation testing data
**/mutants.out*/

# rustc will dump stack traces when hitting an internal compiler error to PWD
rustc-ice-*.txt

# RustRover
#  JetBrains specific template is maintained in a separate JetBrains.gitignore that can
#  be found at https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Global/JetBrains.gitignore
#  and can be added to the global gitignore or merged into this file. However, if you prefer, you
#  could uncomment the following to ignore the entire idea folder.
#.idea/

# OPTIONAL BEGIN library crate -- delete both lines and the entry between them for a binary crate
Cargo.lock
# OPTIONAL END
